gory Food, the toolbar's spent progress portion turns Food's color (olive); Transport → orange.\n\nSo now, the category chip tap opened a text input to rename/create category? Wait, the screenshot shows the text field with \"Transport\" and a keyboard, with \"Category\" area. Hmm, maybe this is the \"chip in edit mode\" — when you tap a category chip that's already selected, you can edit its name? Or perhaps I tapped the \"Category\" chip (add new) because the layout shifted: the chips row might have shifted left when keyboard opened. Actually we tapped element 5 at (862,1047) which was \"Transport\" chip. Hmm.\n\nHold on, maybe what happened: tapping \"Transport\" chip applies the category AND moves the chip to the \"Category\" text field position (i.e., the selected category becomes the text in the \"Category\" field / toolbar?). Hmm.\n\nWait, let's look at the current layout: there's a white pill at y≈1189 containing a tag icon, an EditText \"Transport\" with text selected, and a green check button at right. This is an inline \"category name\" editor. On top of that, the keyboard is shown.\n\nHmm, in the previous observation when I tapped element 5 (Transport at 862,1047), the app may have opened the \"Category\" chip editor because that element's coordinates were mid-animation and landed on the \"Category\" chip (which was at 864,1047 before reorder... yes!). The reorder observations might be due to animations while the app was still settling. Indeed when I tapped Food earlier, elements reordered; I might have tapped during animation.\n\nBut wait, the \"Category\" chip with tag icon was at (864,1047) in the $3 state, and I tapped element 5 which was \"Transport\" at (862,1047). Hmm, in that observe, element 4 Food @(605,1047), element 5 Transport @(862,1047). No Category chip listed! Because Category chip is a text field maybe? Actually the \"Category\" chip disappeared from the list and was replaced by the text field? Hmm.\n\nLook at the state before: after selecting Transport, the chips row showed \"Food\" and \"Transport\" only (no \"Category\" chip). Maybe selecting a category chip turns the chip into an editable field (\"Transport\" with tag icon and check). Actually the white pill with tag icon + editable \"Transport\" text + green check IS the selected category chip in \"edit\" mode? Hmm.\n\nAlternatively, the \"Category\" chip is the selected-category display; when no category selected it shows \"Category\" placeholder with tag icon. Tapping one of the chips applies it and it becomes the \"Category\" field content, editable. That's plausible and explains \"applying a category now also updates the toolbar.\"\n\nBut then why keyboard opened when I tapped? Because tapping the applied category field focuses it for editing (it's an EditText). So my tap likely hit that field (the row moved). Hmm.\n\nOK. This is getting complicated. Let me carefully restart from a clean state and observe the categories flow with screenshots after each tap, waiting for animations.\n\nPress back to dismiss keyboard. Then check state. Actually the \"Transport\" text is selected; maybe I accidentally started renaming Transport. I haven't submitted, so pressing back should discard.\n\nLet me press BACK once (dismiss keyboard), observe."}
