comes focused editable field (keyboard opens) — that could be a UX bug, but not in scope maybe.\n\nLet me look again at observe after tapping Food: element 5 was \"Food\" [clickable] @(903,1047) and element 4 \"Transport\" @(645,1047). No \"Category\" chip. The Food was at right. It was still a View (not EditText) at that point. Then screenshot showed Food chip with tag icon. OK.\n\nIn the observe after tapping Transport (the state with $3), elements [4] Food @(605,1047), [5] Transport @(862,1047) — both Views. Then I tapped element 5. The next state shows EditText \"Transport\" focused. So tapping the applied category chip (Transport, with tag icon) opened its editor. But I intended to tap the Transport chip to select it (before it was already applied? No, before tapping, Transport was NOT applied — Food was still applied? Wait, after clearing input, the toolbar remained olive but what category was applied?). Hmm.\n\nTimeline:\n- Typed 3 → select Transport (tap element 4 at that time, which was \"Transport\" @(383)). After tapping, observe showed Food @(605) then Transport @(862) — so Transport applied (tag chip at right). Toolbar orange (Transport color). Good.\n- Then cleared input ($0), toolbar \"Today $1.4\" olive?? Wait screenshot after clear showed olive \"Today\" pill. But Transport orange should be the color. Hmm! After clearing, toolbar showed olive \"Today\" — that's Food color, not Transport! Wait, was the olive pill from the saved Food expense or from... Hmm.\n\nLet me re-examine: After clearing $3 (Transport selected), the toolbar went back to green with olive \"Today\" pill. If the toolbar color reflects the currently applied category (Transport = orange), it should be orange. It's olive. So maybe the toolbar color reflects the category of the LAST SAVED expense (Food), not the currently selected one. Interesting!\n\nThen typed 1, tapped element 5 (Transport chip) — presumably applied Transport; toolbar turned orange with $0.4 (and 78% fill). So while