{"type": "thinking", "text": "Food's category color is bright green (#7ED957-ish), not olive. So the toolbar pill (olive) is not Food's color either. Therefore the toolbar pill color is not the category color. It's some fixed olive/amber based on spending percentage.\n\nHmm. So the \"toolbar\" in the change note is likely something else entirely. What could \"the toolbar\" be? Maybe the small icon row at top right (Analytics icon, Settings icon) — no.\n\nWait, maybe \"toolbar\" refers to the Analytics screen's top bar? No, that's not on the main screen.\n\nOr maybe \"the toolbar\" is the category chip row itself (the row with chips) — applying a category updates the toolbar (the row) by moving the applied chip to the right / showing the tag icon. The change note: \"Main screen category chip: applying a category now also updates the toolbar.\" Hmm — when you apply a category, the \"toolbar\" could be the toolbar of chips that now shows the applied category. That's exactly what we observed: after applying, the chip with the tag icon (the category field) updates to show the applied category. So the change is that the chip row (toolbar) updates when a category is applied. And that seems to work.\n\nHmm, but that behavior seems trivial. Let me look for other \"toolbar\" elements. Maybe the top bar \"Today €1.4\" is called the \"budget pill\", as the tip says \"hold the budget pill on the home screen to see this anytime\" (from the breakdown sheet). So the top bar is the \"budget pill\". The \"toolbar\" is likely the row above the number pad (the category chips row) — indeed could be called \"toolbar\" in code.\n\nSo the changed feature: applying a category updates the category chip toolbar. Test: after applying a category, the toolbar should show it (chip with tag icon + name). We saw that works: tapping Food → Food chip with tag icon; tapping Transport → Transport chip with tag icon. What about applying a *custom* category by typing in the Category field? Let's test that. Tap the \"Category\" field, type a new category name (e.g., \"Gifts\"), confirm with the check; the toolbar should update to show \"Gifts\" chip. This tests the changed feature more thoroughly.\n\nAlso maybe applying a category via the category chip should update the toolbar's *color*? But we established the pill isn't category colored. So no.\n\nHmm, wait, actually maybe I've been wrong: the pill color might be a fixed \"olive\" for the Today pill and the orange is the \"warning\" color when the *remaining* is low? The orange appears when the pill fills >?? Regardless, we can't verify category colors there.\n\nLet me now check the actual \"toolbar\" == category chip row behavior. The change might have a bug: e.g., after applying a category via the chip, the toolbar (category field) doesn't update if the category was typed manually; or the toolbar shows stale category after clearing the amount; etc.\n\nTest scenarios:\n1. Type amount, apply Food → chip row shows Food with tag. ✓ (observed)\n2. Clear amount (X) → chip row hides; then type again → what category is applied? Earlier, after clearing $3 (Transport applied) and typing again, the row showed Food + Transport(tag)... Let me check: after clearing, does the applied category persist for the next expense? In our latest: after saving the €0.5 Transport, chips hid. Then tap \".\" → row showed Food, Transport, Category (no tag) — wait, after saving, the category reset. Hmm. But earlier after clearing $3, typing 1 showed Food + Transport(tag) — category persisted. Inconsistent? Let me re-examine.\n\nTimeline earlier:\n- Typed 3, tapped Transport → applied.\n- Cleared $3 (X) → main empty, toolbar \"Today $1.4\" olive (had no category).\n- Typed 1 → observed elements: Food (605,1047), Transport (862,1047) — both Views, Transport at right... was Transport applied (tag icon)? The observe didn't show tag icon, but position right suggests applied. Then tapping the Transport chip opened the edit field, implying it was the applied category field. So yes, category persisted across clearing.\n\nAfter saving €0.5 Transport just now, the category reset to none (the row after typing \".\" showed Food, Transport, Category with Category placeholder). So category persists on clear but resets on save? Hmm, maybe persisting is intended (so you can add several expenses in the same category?). Not sure.\n\n3. Cancel: after applying a category then pressing X to clear, tap outside? \n4. Custom category via \"Category\" field: type name, confirm; then the toolbar should show the new category chip. Then save the expense and check the Analytics/list shows the custom category. This also tests data consistency.\n\nLet me test the custom category flow. First go back to main. Currently on Analytics. Press BACK."}
